Public events or information sessions are held regularly on: 
Open Data Day (week): Opening up Geospatial Data - https://data.gov.ro/blog/rezumatul-intalnirii-publice-ziua-datelor-deschise-deschiderea-datelor-geospatiale;
Open Government Week: https://data.gov.ro/blog/rezumatul-intalnirii-prima-strategie-nationala-privind-datele-deschise;
https://data.gov.ro/blog/saptamana-guvernarii-deschise-un-univers-de-date-utile-ins (information session with students on open data and statistical data);
Regular meetings on geo-spatial Data: https://geo-spatial.org/proiecte/seminarii/cluj2024/

In addition to existing measures:
- the Secretariat-General of the Government is also currently conducting a survey on the portal that also includes questions for collecting examples of data re-use (https://forms.gle/6rMkWhmxLfMyd4nq5);
- the draft secondary legislation includes templates for the yearly reporting that mandates the institutions to also monitor re-use through various approaches (https://e-consultare.gov.ro/w/wp-content/plugins/download-attachments/includes/download.php?id=50045; https://e-consultare.gov.ro/w/hotarare-a-guvernului-pentru-aprobarea-normelor-metodologice-de-aplicare-a-legii-nr-179-2022-privind-datele-deschise-si-reutilizarea-informatiilor-din-sectorul-public/);
- when organising events (webinars, public meetings etc.) the SGG also collects re-use examples from participants and promotes those showcases (https://data.gov.ro/blog/rezumatul-intalnirii-publice-ziua-datelor-deschise-deschiderea-datelor-geospatiale);
- the SGG also maintains constant dialogue with re-users.

In addition to existing measures:
- the draft secondary legislation includes templates for the yearly reporting that mandates the institutions to also monitor re-use through various approaches (https://e-consultare.gov.ro/w/wp-content/plugins/download-attachments/includes/download.php?id=50045; https://e-consultare.gov.ro/w/hotarare-a-guvernului-pentru-aprobarea-normelor-metodologice-de-aplicare-a-legii-nr-179-2022-privind-datele-deschise-si-reutilizarea-informatiilor-din-sectorul-public/);
- interactions with public bodies (publication assistance, webinars, meetings, inter-institutional meetings) also include recommendations from the SGG on monitoring re-use at public body level;
- the SGG has also conducted an online survey with open data stewards to collect their practices on various issues, including monitoring of re-use. the results will be used to shape specific actions in the Strategy's Action Plan.
